Context from prior work:
Goal: Enhance TaskForge CLI with a gate summarizer to compress historical task data and decompose goals into subtasks for RazorCascade memory study efficiency.
Decisions: Use Commander for CLI subcommands and hooks; Implement atomic JSON persistence with Bun's file API; Validate data with Zod schemas for integrity; Add pre-action hooks for summarization in flagship commands
Risks: Performance may exceed 500ms for >10k tasks; Concurrency could corrupt summary files without locking; Decomposition accuracy may be imprecise with rule-based logic
Snippets: async function summarizeHistory(tasksFile: string = './taskforge-tasks.json'): Promise<z.infer<typeof SummarySchema>> {
  const tasks = JSON.parse(await readFile(tasksFile, 'utf-8'));
  const compressed = tasks.reduce((acc: Record<string, number>, task: any) => {
    acc[task.status] = (acc[task.status] || 0) + 1;
    return acc;
  }, {});
  const subtasks = tasks.filter(t => t.status === 'pending').map(t => `Subtask: ${t.description}`);
  const summary = { compressedHistory: Object.entries(compressed).map(([status, count]) => ({ status, count })), subtasks };
  return SummarySchema.parse(summary);
}
